## Group D — CSV imports, the common mechanics ✅

**`GroupDIT.java`** written from scratch (no prior class to complete). Campaign is **BUILD SUCCESS** — `Tests run: 9, Failures: 0, Skipped: 1`.

**Tiering** — all of D1–D9 are unmarked in the catalog → the whole group is `@QuarkusTest` + RestAssured, HTTP Basic (`admin/admin`, plus a MANAGER for D9). **No mirror seed needed** — every scenario imports its own throwaway rows through the dependency-free `/stores/import` (and `/prices/import` for D4).

| | Scenario | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| D1 | nominal + blank lines ignored | ✅ |
| D2 | not-enough-columns error / extra cols accepted | ✅ |
| D3 | malformed error-JSON de-facto contract | ✅ |
| D4 | leading blank line shifts header into data | ✅ |
| D5 | staged transactional fallback (24 survive, 1 isolated) | ✅ |
| D6 | checksum idempotence (`updated_at` untouched) | ✅ |
| D7 | in-file duplicate key, last line wins | ✅ |
| D8 | stream 500s | ⏭ justified `@Disabled` residue |
| D9 | MANAGER → 403 on all 7 import endpoints | ✅ |

**Two iterations to green:** (1) fixed a `{@code /*/import}` in Javadoc whose `*/` closed the comment and broke compilation; (2) calibrated D5 — the faulty 13th data row reports as **`Line 14`** (header is physical line 1) and the isolated message is the Narayana commit wrapper `ARJUNA016053: Could not commit transaction.`, not the raw `@NotBlank` text.

**Key calibration findings** (full detail in `reports/e2e-D.md`): D3's malformed JSON confirmed (missing opening quote on the first error → textual-only asserts); D4's "header-as-data business error" is resource-dependent, so `/prices/import` was chosen to surface it faithfully; the staged-fallback WARN log is emitted but not asserted (the 24-survivors + isolated-line pair is the observable proof). D8 is the sole residue: `IOException`/`Throwable` stream faults aren't injectable through a well-formed RestAssured request.

