## Summary

Created `src/test/java/com/intermarche/valuation/e2e/GroupKIT.java` (new class) covering all **9 scenarios K1–K9** from the "Remises — bons immédiats & vignettes" section, plus the report at `reports/e2e-K.md`.

**Result:** `Tests run: 9, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0` — **BUILD SUCCESS**, green on the first campaign run (all amounts derived from source before writing, no calibration re-runs).

**Tiering:** all 9 are unmarked → `@QuarkusTest` + RestAssured, Basic `admin/admin`. No `[W]`/`[P]` scenarios, so no Playwright/prod-like harness. The mirror seed was needed (both discount engines price against real catalog prices), replayed once in the mandated 7-import order plus three additive phases.

**Key calibration findings (catalog vs. code):**
- The discounted standard line is priced on **`BASE_FOR_DISCOUNT`, not `DEFAULT`** — `BasicOfferApplier` switches to `refPrice` the moment a discount applier registers on it. This drives every K1/K2/K3/K5/K6 base amount (apple base `0.99`/`1.19`, not `0.90`/`1.08`).
- K1 graves the historic "wrong-sign" regression as GREEN (two vouchers stack, both reduce → `0.74`/`0.89`); K2/K6 grave the uncapped-formula negative totals to the cent.
- **K7 & K8 both surface under `Error building appliers from factory:`** — K8's `/ by zero` fires during the early efficiency-score `apply()` inside `createOfferAppliers`, before the apply-time wrapper. The test asserts the invariant substring `/ by zero`, which holds either way.
- K4 (the "couture") is proven as a pure retrieval-method contrast: store-only types (IMMEDIATE_VOUCHER, DEPOSIT_BASKET) ignore a group attach; store+group types (N+M, MIXED_BUNDLE, VIGNETTE) honour it — 5 of the 8 types probed, the other 3 documented residue sharing the identical `findByStoreAndType`/`getOffers` methods.

Per the workflow, I did **not** commit — the campaign script owns the commit. Untracked scaffolding files (`campaign-*.log`, `run-*.sh`, `OfferGraphQLClientTest.java`, `GroupBIT.java`, etc.) were left as they were.
