## Summary

Wrote `src/test/java/com/intermarche/valuation/e2e/GroupLIT.java` (new class) covering all **7 scenarios** of the L section — livraison, consigne, franco de port — plus the report at `reports/e2e-L.md`. Campaign: **`Tests run: 7, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` — BUILD SUCCESS**, 2 iterations to green.

**Scenarios (all RestAssured, pure HTTP, Basic admin/admin):**
- **L1** nominal `HOME_DELIVERY` (Seclin → 9.90€ tier, no valued items, total 15.90/13.25)
- **L2** distance beyond every tier → no delivery, 200, merchandise valued
- **L3** four coordinate guards (no address / address without lat-lon / no-offer store / no-coord store `0199`), asserted on `valuation_traces.error_message`
- **L4** PICKUP/IN_STORE/absent modes → no delivery even with address
- **L5** second DELIVERY + second DEPOSIT_BASKET → `Multiple … offers` 500
- **L6** consigne (trimmed/case-insensitive instruction → `2 x 0.5€`, no-instruction/zero-volume → nothing)
- **L7** franco (above → full 9.90 refund capped, below → kept, no-delivery → nothing)

**Seed:** mirror catalog replayed once + 3 additive extra phases (store `0199` with empty coords, mirrored `…005` prices on `0104`/`0199`, and the L5 double-offer poisons quarantined on `0104`).

**Key calibration findings (catalog vs reality):**
- Seclin is **10.23 km**, not the catalog's ~11 km — still in the 16 km tier; `%.2f` is locale-formatted (comma under fr_FR) so the type is asserted by prefix + suffix.
- Type strings **drop trailing zeros** (`9.9€`, `0.5€`) via `BigDecimal.toString()`; the numeric amounts stay exact — the only recalibration between runs.
- L5 message carries `'0104'` (quarantine store), format verbatim; catalog quoted `'0101'`.
- L7 tiers are **FIXED_AMOUNT 50/100**, not percentages — both cap to the 9.90€ delivery, so the tier distinction is inert.
- Group franco (`PROMO_GROUP_NORD`) is dead (store-only retrieval).

**Residue:** none. No `[W]`/`[P]` scenarios in the L section. No `src/main` changes; only the new IT class, its seed resources (inline), and the report were touched. Not committed — per the workflow the campaign script owns the commit.
