## Summary

Created `src/test/java/com/intermarche/valuation/e2e/GroupNIT.java` (new class) covering all **7 catalog scenarios** of section **N — Traces & administration des valorisations**, plus the Q-E "Valuations" message surface. Campaign is green:

```
Tests run: 16, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 3 — BUILD SUCCESS
```

**Tiering** (16 @Test, 13 active + 3 @Disabled [W] residues):
- **N1** (4 tests) — the four statuses' exact content. 200/400/500 over HTTP asserting `valuation_traces` columns via Panache; the **HTTP-unreachable 422+responsePayload arm and the 1997-char truncation** exercised through the injected `ValuationTraceService.record` with a genuine `engine.evaluate` result.
- **N2** — disable → zero trace + off-banner + immediate re-enable.
- **N3** — retention validation notices + VIEWER/MANAGER `403` on config & purge.
- **N4** (2) — manual `Purge all now` 303; scheduled purge via antedated `createdAt` (`DateTimeProvider`) + a direct `purgeExpired()` call.
- **N5/N6/N7** — full **server surface** over HTTP (filters/badges/empty state, `/rows` refresh source, detail meta/error-banner/no-response/303-unknown-id, test-form empty/400/success + trace creation, replay preload & silent-empty), with the pure-JS behaviours (`valuation-refresh.js`, `valuation-view.js`, `schema-form.js`) as 3 justified `@Disabled` [W] residues.

**Key calibrations:** N1's 422 is unreachable via the contract (confirmed against G3); N1's `requestPayload` is the re-serialized basket so an unknown wire field is dropped; and the single red→green fix — N5's filter value is **echoed into the search input**, making `body.contains(customer)` a false positive on empty pages, so positives assert on the row badge and the strict-status mismatch asserts the empty-state message.

Report written to `reports/e2e-N.md`. Nothing under `src/main` was touched; no commit made (the campaign script owns that).

One note on the `[W]` tier: there's **no `quarkus-playwright` dependency in the build**, and adding it falls outside this task's scope (touch only `GroupNIT.java`, its resources, and the report). I therefore covered every server-side surface of the [W] scenarios over HTTP and disabled only the irreducibly-browser behaviours — rather than adding the dependency myself.
